<title>USA: US Army awards four major engineering contracts.</title>
<headline>US Army awards four major engineering contracts.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Army said Wednesday it has awarded contracts that could total nearly $3 billion for Army Strategic Defense Command systems engineering to MEVATEC Corp, Nichols Research Corp., Computer Science Corp. and Teledyne Brown Engineering.</p>
<p>It said it was paying the first increments of contracts that could total $834 million for MEVATEC, $649 million for Nichols Research, $737 million for Computer Science and $745 million for Teledyne Brown. Computer Science announced its contract Tuesday.</p>
</text>
